        "original_id": "aaec07da-ab76-5ac1-b717-4ba0aec29b04",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Felix Avenue, Marcos Highway, Ortigas Avenue Extension, National Arts Center, Cainta, Philippines\n- People: Francisco P. Felix, Imelda Marcos, Ferdinand Marcos\n- Roles: mayor of Cainta, First Lady, President, politician\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, First Lady Imelda Marcos inaugurated the National Arts Center.\n- Felix Avenue, also known as Imelda Avenue, is a four-lane major road that connects Marcos Highway to Ortigas Avenue Extension.\n- Felix Avenue is named after Francisco P. Felix, a former mayor of Cainta, and Imelda Marcos, the wife of former President Ferdinand Marcos and a former First Lady.\n- Imelda Marcos remains one of the richest politicians in the Philippines through her collection of clothing, artwork, and jewelry, along with money in offshore bank accounts under the pseudonym \"Jane Ryan\".",
